Cell["\<\
For the representative choice (a,b)=(1,2), y3=-2 log(delta), y4=O(1), and \
y5=2 log(delta). Thus y3 >> y4 >> y5. At the same time p4 is genuinely soft: \
both of its light-cone components and its transverse momentum vanish as \
delta. This violates the generic-MRK condition that all three transverse \
momenta be comparable, while preserving the multi-Regge rapidity ordering.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a192efe9-2985-4d3a-9259-6fee10ea5852"],

Cell["\<\
The leading terms reproduce the Section-2 MRK variables with s=P M, s2=(P \
R/K) delta^a, s1=(K M) delta^a and s1 s2/s=R delta^(2a). Unlike a \
leading-only substitution, this exact chart retains every subleading layer \
that asymptotic-order alignment may promote.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"494f6c46-972c-484d-ab3e-29b25ea2fb8a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      TagBox["s12",
       HoldForm], "\[Rule]", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"M", " ", "P"}], 
       SuperscriptBox["delta", "4"]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      TagBox["s34",
       HoldForm], "\[Rule]", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"P", " ", "R"}], 
       RowBox[{"delta", " ", "K"}]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      TagBox["s45",
       HoldForm], "\[Rule]", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"K", " ", "M"}], "delta"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      TagBox["s23",
       HoldForm], "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"-", "T"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      TagBox["s15",
       HoldForm], "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"C", " ", "delta"}]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["delta", "2"], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"-", "R"}], ")"}]}], "-", "T"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      TagBox[
       SuperscriptBox[
        TemplateBox[{"p4perp"},
         "Abs"], "2"],
       HoldForm], "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["delta", "2"], " ", "R"}]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b6c1f2d1-9e49-49d1-9b2a-\
46e137bc3e79"],

Cell["\<\
The apparently unusual invariant powers follow immediately. In ordinary MRK \
with x=delta^2, s1 and s2 are fixed and s34,s45 scale as delta^(-2). In the \
central-soft path, s1 and s2 themselves scale as delta, so s34=s2/x and \
s45=s1/x scale only as delta^(-1). The transfers s23 and s15 remain finite; \
s15 is not a large subenergy.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0ddaef5f-7389-4e76-9bbb-241cf7f3ffb6"],

