Cell["Why a four-valent attachment is necessary", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"fafee682-96a8-4055-a708-fac46c38fa48"],

Cell["\<\
The distinction is already visible on the leading face exposed by the natural \
alignment phi=(-3,-3,0,-3,-3,-3). When p4 is emitted from the trivalent \
middle vertex 4, the aligned face is\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ad7344f7-92d5-4842-8e7f-0d58e7422672"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["F", "mid", "align"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"Q4hat2", " ", "x1", " ", "X45hat", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x4", " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"x2", " ", "X34hat"}], "-", "x3"}], ")"}]}], "+", 
         RowBox[{"x2", " ", "X34hat", " ", "x5"}]}], ")"}]}], 
      RowBox[{"zetaBarHat", " ", "zetaHat"}]]}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"1283b273-103c-479c-bb70-\
3d8e1f6f7e72"],

Cell["\<\
The bracket may vanish for positive parameters, but its x5 derivative is \
X34hat x2>0. Hence the zero is not stationary and is not a positive Landau \
pinch. The unmatched term X34hat x2 x5 records that the soft leg was inserted \
in the middle of one particular theta path.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"83ca4143-d148-4ccf-8345-142eab9c958f"],

Cell["\<\
When p4 is attached instead to the four-valent theta endpoint 5, the \
corresponding face factorizes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ea369b53-90d3-4d4d-89ee-ea0f919375e0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["F", "end", "align"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"Q4hat2", " ", "X45hat", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x2", " ", "X34hat"}], "-", "x3"}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x1", " ", "x4"}], "-", 
         RowBox[{"x0", " ", "x5"}]}], ")"}]}], 
      RowBox[{"zetaBarHat", " ", "zetaHat"}]]}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"5ff89ae6-0885-434c-9b30-\
57a9a162d9a3"],

Cell["\<\
The simultaneous zero of the two routing differences is stationary: for a \
product A B, d(A B)=B dA+A dB vanishes when A=B=0. At the endpoint all three \
theta paths remain available, so the two-loop flow can rebalance in two \
independent ways. Inserting p4 in the middle of a path distinguishes that \
path and prevents the second rebalancing. The full twelve-attachment scan \
confirms that no alternative aligned face restores a pinch for a trivalent \
attachment.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1286b2ce-8853-4197-9029-77ed6030b9d3"],

