Cell["\<\
The displayed polynomial is the coefficient of the delta^(-10) layer after \
alignment alone. The immediately following layer remains nonzero on the \
cancellation locus:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9a4559df-4c66-4708-8f87-3e3928be8eca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["F", 
     RowBox[{"-", "9"}], "align"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"Q4hat2", " ", "x0", " ", "x3", " ", "x4"}], 
      RowBox[{"zetaBarHat", " ", "zetaHat"}]]}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"9c6c648b-bba1-4256-b054-\
19f354aae6c4"],

Cell["\<\
The alignment vector is phi=(-3,-3,0,-3,-3,-3), and the second-stage HRF \
vector is rho=(-1,-1,-1,-1,-1,-1). Their composition gives the \
hard-scale-normalized region vector \
(x0,x1,x2,x3,x4,x5;delta)=(-4,-4,-1,-4,-4,-4;1), with (W_SL,W_HR)=(-9,-8). \
Factoring out the growing hard scale s12 defines this dimensionless \
convention. Adding +4 uniformly converts to dimensionful Schwinger parameters \
while s12 varies, but that non-negative representative is not the infrared \
HRF vector. The resolved support has affine rank 6, equal to the required \
rank, so this is one scaleful lower facet. The other two staged presentations \
fail that final test.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f170221-0de3-4eb4-9bde-71ef30d5de2d"],

Cell["Opposite four-valent endpoint", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ed86a8ad-4c4a-4582-a95b-de435c440539"],

Cell["\<\
Moving p4 from endpoint 5 to the directly reflected endpoint 3, while \
reflecting the endpoint attachment of p3, gives the ordering {1,2,4,5,3}. A \
separate full-native-layer run again has three staged candidates; two are \
rejected as scaleless and one is a rank-six lower facet. Its fixed-edge \
vector differs from the representative vector:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3a55accb-1fd6-4f1a-8c70-b61f46f270dc"],

