Cell["\<\
Both four-valent endpoints carry a t-channel Glauber transfer. They do not \
define two loop modes: the second transfer is an affine rerouting of the \
first, ell_second=p1-p5-ell_first, so their local fluctuations obey Delta \
ell_second=-Delta ell_first.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"49393157-9456-4a1b-8c7b-2785babddc4f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"attachment\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"first t-channel routing\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"first central powers\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"second t-channel routing\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"second central powers\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"local relation\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"independent Glauber loops\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"p4 at endpoint 5\"\>", "\<\"ell3=q0-q4=p3-q2\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{2, 2, 0}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"], "\<\"ell5=q1-q5=p4-q3\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{4, 1, 1}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"], "\<\"Delta ell5=-Delta ell3\"\>", "1"},
    {"\<\"p4 at endpoint 3\"\>", "\<\"ell5=q1-q5=p3-q3\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{2, 2, 0}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"], "\<\"ell3=q0-q4=p4-q2\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{4, 1, 1}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"], "\<\"Delta ell3=-Delta ell5\"\>", "1"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.1}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"549178ae-7956-4e9a-bfd0-924fc1479b04"],

Cell["\<\
The mode tests are: 1+3=2*2 for the on-shell-balanced soft-collinear edge; \
-2+3<2*2 for the longitudinal-dominated edge; and 4+1>2*2 for the local \
widths of the Glauber loop ell. Thus Glauber character belongs to the loop \
combination ell, not to an individual propagator.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f887808a-8162-413f-b66e-a468c371b5e4"],

Cell["\<\
For both attachments q0/q1 pinch the ordinary plus component at width \
delta^4, q4/q5 pinch the Glauber plus component at delta^4, and q2/q3 \
restrict its minus component to delta. Both transverse widths are delta^2. \
Since 4+1>2*2, there is precisely one Glauber loop, presented in two \
t-channel affine routings through the two theta endpoints.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5d99d8d8-73ad-4861-82b9-3a1e6e19faa3"],

Cell["\<\
In parameter space the representative normals are A=P x2-K delta^3 x3 and \
B=x1 x4-x0 x5. For the opposite endpoint A becomes K delta^3 x2-P x3, while B \
is unchanged. In each case wt(A)=0, wt(B)=-8, four tangential coordinates \
contribute -16 and the Jacobian contributes +4, giving measure power -20. In \
momentum space the ordinary and Glauber measures give 2D and 2D+1; the six \
propagator powers sum to 21.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3c81f957-686f-44dc-a321-ec276be705a6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"attachment\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"parameter measure\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"momentum measure\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"sum q_e^2 powers\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"scalar power\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"endpoint 5\"\>", 
     RowBox[{"-", "20"}], "\<\"4D+1\"\>", 
     "21", "\<\"4D-20=-4-8 epsilon\"\>"},
    {"\<\"endpoint 3\"\>", 
     RowBox[{"-", "20"}], "\<\"4D+1\"\>", "21", "\<\"4D-20=-4-8 epsilon\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.1}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"2838c9e8-95bd-4196-8751-ff448e787a3a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[ImaginaryI]", "CS", "scalar"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox["delta", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "D"}], "-", "20"}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox["delta", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"8", " ", "epsilon"}]}], "-", "4"}]]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"fe0ab73d-cabf-437b-a742-\
6dd363e65580"],

Cell["\<\
The two representations therefore agree for the dimensionless integral with \
s12 factored out. Restoring the overall engineering-dimension factor \
s12^(D-6) is a separate conversion and must not be used to redefine the \
infrared region vector.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"80d77411-b915-4b4d-bce4-45bfd205f0bf"],

Cell["7. Negative controls and interpretation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7fff77f4-4a08-411a-99a3-beba3548fc8f"],

Cell["\<\
All twelve one-loop pentagon labelings fail already at the recursive \
mixed-derivative pinch preselection for each of the three tested rates. \
Generic MRK gives no certified HR for any labeling of the two-loop seed: six \
labelings produce staged near-misses, but the lower-facet audit rejects them. \
In the exact central-soft chart, all six accepted labelings attach p4 to a \
four-valent seed vertex, but the endpoint condition alone is not sufficient: \
{1,3,2,5,4} is an endpoint attachment with no surviving face.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8ef6e63e-4975-467e-8398-fded9442e6ba"],

Cell["\<\
This establishes that the earlier blanket statement 'there is no HR in \
five-point MRK' is not correct once the central-soft composite limit is \
included. What is established here is narrower: one specific two-loop seed \
family and all its inequivalent external labelings. A topology scan of its \
vertex-split descendants is the natural next step.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"08b8f5ed-b621-4ff5-b807-e9263dea8c31"],

Cell["8. Reproduction", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"66454a92-0bb7-4f31-9544-12c53630126a"],

